      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for checking that. but that's the thing—i checked the mission schedules for the whole sector and none of these sats are scheduled for station-keeping or any maneuvers tonight. they should be on a smooth path.\n\nand it's not just the timing. if you look at the delta values, they're too identical. in real orbital mechanics, even tiny drag variables make them slightly different. it feels like a heartbeat or a signal being pulsed. \n\ncould this be a way of transmitting data through position shifts? like, instead of radio waves, they're using the actual orbital path to send a coded message that's harder to intercept? what would a sequence like that even look like if it were a cipher?",
